IMPORT prelude

-- CareShield Life and Long-Term Care Act 2019 (Singapore) -- who is automatically covered by CareShield Life (s 6(1)(a), (b)), the
-- meaning of "severely disabled" and "not disabled" (First and Fourth Schedules), entitlement to the monthly insured sum and when
-- it ends (ss 12, 18(7)), refusal of a claim (s 16(4)), the premium deadline (s 14(3)), the cap on late-payment penalties (s 29(3)),
-- protection of payouts from creditors (s 20), the proper claimant of a deceased payer's cash premium (s 15(3), (5)), joint moneys
-- held by a defaulter's agent (s 25(3), (9)), the bar on leaving Singapore (s 28(6)), change of address (s 58), and the offences of
-- false declarations (s 48) and misuse of payouts (s 50), with composition (s 56).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CLLTCA2019.txt. The cover says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". Later amendments are annotated in
-- the text, the latest being Act 18 of 2025 (CareShield Life and Long-Term Care (Amendment) Act 2025, commencement 1 January 2026),
-- the last entry in the deposited legislative history. SSO's metadata calls it the "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: CareShield Life is the compulsory long-term care insurance that covers
-- Singapore citizens and permanent residents born in or after 1980 from age 30, paid for from MediSave, and paying a monthly sum
-- on severe disability. SCOPED to what an insured person, a payer or a caregiver meets. Not encoded: coverage under s 6(1)(c) and
-- (d) (both turn on prescribed dates, periods and conditions, none retrieved) and the Board's discretion in s 6(4); the
-- ElderShield transfer (Part 3) beyond noting it; the amount of any premium or insured sum (prescribed, not in the Act);
-- deferment and suspension (s 19); demand notes, defaulter's agents and suits beyond the provisions named above (ss 23-27);
-- restricted information (Part 8); the Funds and the Council (Parts 9, 10); investigators (ss 46, 47); fraudulent assessments
-- (s 49); and any regulations.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the example naive rows. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `CareShield Life and Long-Term Care Act 2019 -- CareShield Life`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `First and Fourth Schedules -- severely disabled and not disabled`

-- First Schedule: "a person is severely disabled when he or she is unable to perform 3 or more of the following activities of daily
-- living": (a) washing; (b) dressing; (c) feeding; (d) toileting; (e) walking or moving (Act 18 of 2025); (f) transferring.
-- Fourth Schedule (Act 18 of 2025): "a person is not disabled only if he or she can perform all of the following activities of
-- daily living without assistance all the time" -- the same six.
-- The two tests are of different kinds: one counts activities the person is UNABLE to perform, the other asks whether any activity
-- needs assistance at any time. A person who needs help with one or two activities is neither. The encoding takes two counts:
-- activities the person cannot perform at all, and activities the person cannot perform without assistance all the time.
GIVEN `activities the person is unable to perform` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is severely disabled` IF
    `activities the person is unable to perform` AT LEAST 3

GIVEN `activities needing assistance at some time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is not disabled` IF
    `activities needing assistance at some time` EQUALS 0

§§ `6(1)(a), (b) -- who CareShield Life applies to without applying`

-- s 6(1)(a): "every citizen of Singapore or permanent resident of Singapore whose birthday is on or after 1 January 1980 and who is
-- at least 30 years of age". No condition as to health.
-- s 6(1)(b) (as amended by Act 18 of 2025): every individual (i) "who, on 30 September 2020, was not a citizen of Singapore or a
-- permanent resident of Singapore, but becomes" one "on or after 1 October 2020"; (ii) "whose birthday is before 1 January 1980";
-- and (iii) who, if the SCPR date is on or after commencement of s 3(a) of the 2025 amending Act, "is not disabled on that SCPR
-- date", or, if before it, "was not severely disabled on that SCPR date".
-- The commencement of s 3(a) of the 2025 Act is taken to be 1 January 2026, the date annotated against the amended text (an
-- inference: the deposit gives one commencement date for Act 18 of 2025 and does not list its sections separately).
-- s 2(1) "SCPR date": the date the individual becomes a citizen or a permanent resident, "whichever occurs first".
GIVEN `a citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN, `born on or after 1 January 1980` IS A BOOLEAN, `age in years` IS A NUMBER,
      `first became a citizen or PR on or after 1 October 2020` IS A BOOLEAN, `SCPR date on or after 1 January 2026` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `activities unable to perform on the SCPR date` IS A NUMBER, `activities needing assistance on the SCPR date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `CareShield Life applies automatically` IF
        `a citizen or permanent resident`
    AND (    (`born on or after 1 January 1980` AND `age in years` AT LEAST 30)
         OR  (    (NOT `born on or after 1 January 1980`)
              AND `first became a citizen or PR on or after 1 October 2020`
              AND IF `SCPR date on or after 1 January 2026`
                  THEN `the person is not disabled` `activities needing assistance on the SCPR date`
                  ELSE NOT `the person is severely disabled` `activities unable to perform on the SCPR date`))

§§ `12, 16(4), 18(7) -- the insured sum`

-- s 12(2): an insured person "is entitled to one or more payments of an insured sum of an amount prescribed where (a) the insured
-- person is severely disabled; and (b) a claim made by or on behalf of the insured person is accepted under section 16".
-- s 12(3): entitlement ends (a) when cover ends in accordance with the regulations, or (b) otherwise, "on the date that the insured
-- person is no longer severely disabled".
-- s 18(7): "Despite section 12(3)(b), the Board may continue to make payment ... until the completion of the insured person's next
-- periodic disability review mentioned in section 21."
GIVEN `an insured person` IS A BOOLEAN, `activities unable to perform` IS A NUMBER, `claim accepted` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `cover has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is entitled to the insured sum` IF
        `an insured person`
    AND `the person is severely disabled` `activities unable to perform`
    AND `claim accepted`
    AND (NOT `cover has ended`)

GIVEN `claim accepted` IS A BOOLEAN, `cover has ended` IS A BOOLEAN, `activities unable to perform` IS A NUMBER,
      `next periodic review completed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may pay the insured sum` IF
        `claim accepted`
    AND (NOT `cover has ended`)
    AND (    `the person is severely disabled` `activities unable to perform`
         OR  (NOT `next periodic review completed`))

-- s 16(4): the Administrator "may refuse a claim" (a) if the insured person is not severely disabled; (b) if the claim is not made
-- in accordance with the section (form, manner, documents); (c) on non-compliance with a request or a requirement to attend a
-- disability assessment under (3); or (d) if the severe disability "arises from one or more such events or occurrences as may be
-- prescribed" (none retrieved).
GIVEN `activities unable to perform` IS A NUMBER, `claim in the required form with documents` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `complied with requests and assessment` IS A BOOLEAN, `disability from a prescribed excluded event` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Administrator may refuse the claim` IF
        (NOT `the person is severely disabled` `activities unable to perform`)
    OR  (NOT `claim in the required form with documents`)
    OR  (NOT `complied with requests and assessment`)
    OR  `disability from a prescribed excluded event`

§§ `14(3), 29(3) -- paying the premium`

-- s 14(3): the premium must be paid "not later than 30 days after the beginning of the relevant insurance period, or on or before a
-- later date the Board may permit in any particular case". (4): the Board may deduct it from the insured person's MediSave.
GIVEN `days after the insurance period began` IS A NUMBER, `later day permitted by the Board` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the premium is paid in time` IF
    `days after the insurance period began` AT MOST `the greater of` 30 `later day permitted by the Board`

-- s 29(3): "The total amount of the penalties imposed on the premium and interest for an insurance period must not exceed 17% of the
-- total amount of the premium for that insurance period and any interest imposed under section 23(1)(a)". The rates themselves are
-- prescribed and were not retrieved.
GIVEN `the premium` IS A NUMBER, `interest imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the late-payment penalties can total` MEANS
    (`the premium` PLUS `interest imposed`) TIMES 17 DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `15(3), (5) -- a cash payer who dies before the period starts`

-- s 15(3): where a person who paid "in cash" any sum towards a premium "dies before the start of that insurance period", and the sum
-- does not exceed an amount the Minister specifies by Gazette notification (not retrieved), the Board may pay "a proper claimant".
-- (5) "proper claimant": (a) the personal representative; or (b) one claiming as "the widower, widow, child, grandchild, parent,
-- brother, sister, nephew, niece, grandparent, uncle or aunt of the deceased". "parent" includes an adoptive parent, a
-- step-parent, a guardian or a person with actual custody; "child" includes a child adopted by court order.
DECLARE Claimant IS ONE OF
    `the personal representative`
    `the widow or widower`
    `a child`
    `an adopted child`
    `a grandchild`
    `a step-parent`
    `a brother or sister`
    `a nephew or niece`
    `an uncle or aunt`
    `a cousin`
    `a friend who paid the funeral`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be a proper claimant` IF
    CONSIDER `the claimant`
    WHEN `a cousin` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a friend who paid the funeral` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `20 -- payouts are protected from creditors`

-- s 20(1): benefits paid to or for an insured person (a) "are not assignable or transferable, and not liable to be attached,
-- sequestered or levied upon"; (b) "are excluded from any set-off of any nature for any debt", except under (2); (c) on bankruptcy
-- do not pass to the Official Assignee.
-- s 20(2): (1)(b) does not apply to set-off of "(a) any debt due to the Fund; and (b) any debt arising from the care of the insured
-- person and due to the healthcare institution that is an approved payee receiving the benefits on behalf of the insured person who
-- is receiving care from the healthcare institution".
DECLARE Debt IS ONE OF
    `a debt due to the CareShield Fund`
    `care fees owed to the nursing home that is the approved payee`
    `care fees owed to a nursing home that is not the approved payee`
    `an unrelated debt owed to the nursing home that is the approved payee`
    `a credit card debt`
    `a debt of the family member receiving the payout`

GIVEN `the debt` IS A Debt
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the payout may be set off against the debt` IF
    CONSIDER `the debt`
    WHEN `a debt due to the CareShield Fund` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `care fees owed to the nursing home that is the approved payee` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `25(3), (9) -- joint moneys`

-- s 25(3): "It is presumed, until the contrary is proved, that the joint account holders of a joint account have equal shares of the
-- moneys in the account". (9): "joint account" means a bank account in the names of 2 or more persons, "but excludes any partnership
-- account, any trust account and any account where a minor is one of the joint account holders".
GIVEN `holders` IS A NUMBER, `a partnership account` IS A BOOLEAN, `a trust account` IS A BOOLEAN, `a minor is a holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a joint account under section 25` IF
        `holders` AT LEAST 2
    AND (NOT `a partnership account`)
    AND (NOT `a trust account`)
    AND (NOT `a minor is a holder`)

GIVEN `the balance` IS A NUMBER, `holders` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the defaulter's presumed share` MEANS `the balance` DIVIDED BY `holders`

§§ `28(6) -- leaving Singapore with premiums unpaid`

-- s 28(6): a defaulter who, "knowing that a direction has been issued under this section to prevent the defaulter's departure",
-- "voluntarily leaves or attempts to leave Singapore without paying the outstanding premium or furnishing security" commits an
-- offence: fine up to $5,000, imprisonment up to 12 months, or both; and may be arrested without warrant.
GIVEN `knows of the direction` IS A BOOLEAN, `leaves or attempts to leave voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `security furnished` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `leaving is an offence under section 28` IF
        `knows of the direction`
    AND `leaves or attempts to leave voluntarily`
    AND (NOT `paid`)
    AND (NOT `security furnished`)

§§ `58 -- change of address`

-- s 58(1): an insured person liable to pay premium, a person liable to pay on their behalf, and every person who receives a benefit
-- "must inform the Board or the Administrator in writing of any change" of residential address. (2): a person who has reported the
-- change "under section 10 of the National Registration Act 1965" is taken to have informed the Board. The Act states no penalty
-- for breach of s 58.
GIVEN `wrote to the Board or Administrator` IS A BOOLEAN, `reported under the National Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has informed the Board of the new address` IF
    `wrote to the Board or Administrator` OR `reported under the National Registration Act`

§§ `48 -- false or misleading declarations and claims`

-- s 48(1): knowingly making or assisting a false or misleading health declaration, means declaration, claim or application; a
-- knowingly misleading omission; or knowingly supplying false information that may be used in one.
-- (2): on conviction, "(a) in the case where the person is an individual -- to a penalty equal to the relevant amount; or (b) in
-- any other case -- to a penalty equal to 5 times the relevant amount". No fine and no imprisonment under (2).
-- (3): with "the intention of causing any premium to be undercharged or any benefit or claim to be overpaid": an individual, fine up
-- to $5,000 or 12 months or both, "and in addition" a penalty of 2 times the relevant amount; any other person, fine up to $10,000
-- and a penalty of 4 times.
-- (4) "relevant amount": the premium undercharged or benefit overpaid, "or that would have been" had the declaration been accepted.
-- The Act does not say whether a person convicted under (3) also faces the (2) penalty; the encoding treats (3) as replacing (2)
-- (an inference).
GIVEN `an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `intended undercharge or overpayment` IS A BOOLEAN, `the relevant amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 48 penalty` MEANS
    IF `intended undercharge or overpayment`
    THEN IF `an individual` THEN 2 TIMES `the relevant amount` ELSE 4 TIMES `the relevant amount`
    ELSE IF `an individual` THEN `the relevant amount` ELSE 5 TIMES `the relevant amount`

GIVEN `an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `intended undercharge or overpayment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 48 maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `intended undercharge or overpayment`
    THEN IF `an individual` THEN 5000 ELSE 10000
    ELSE 0

§§ `50 -- misuse of payouts`

-- s 50(1): a person who receives benefits "on behalf of an insured person must first apply the benefits for the care of the insured
-- person". (2): contravention "without reasonable excuse" is an offence: an individual, fine up to $10,000 or 2 years or both, and
-- a penalty of 4 times the relevant amount; any other person, fine up to $20,000 and 8 times. (3): the court may order repayment
-- into the Fund with interest. (4) "relevant amount": the benefits received "which was not applied for the care of the insured
-- person".
GIVEN `receives benefits on behalf of the insured person` IS A BOOLEAN, `applied them first for the insured person's care` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an offence of misusing the payout` IF
        `receives benefits on behalf of the insured person`
    AND (NOT `applied them first for the insured person's care`)
    AND (NOT `a reasonable excuse`)

GIVEN `an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `amount not applied for care` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 50 penalty` MEANS
    IF `an individual` THEN 4 TIMES `amount not applied for care` ELSE 8 TIMES `amount not applied for care`

GIVEN `an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 50 maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `an individual` THEN 10000 ELSE 20000

§§ `56 -- composition`

-- s 56(1): an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of the following:
-- (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $1,000." Which offences are prescribed was
-- not retrieved.
GIVEN `the maximum fine for the offence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a composition can be` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the maximum fine for the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 1000
